 and the slice spacing is 1.25 mm. This further supports a diameter around 4-5 mm, which feels right given my visual assessment.\n\nSo, I'm going with 4 mm. The key here is to make it a discrete, consistent value, or a tight range. 4 mm it is. All in all, this has to be a Nodule. It is certainly not a vessel.\n\nMy response:\n\nNodule. The structure is a discrete, rounded opacity that appears and disappears over a few slices, lacking the continuous tubular appearance of a vessel. 4 mm."
